I did some experiments and can repo the issue on clusters >= 1.27.

It looks like the issue is the value in node.cpu.usageNanoCores is incorrect as retured by the /stats/summary endpoint (and this value matches the incorrect value returned by `kubectl top node`)

I set up two clusters and ran a container that consumes ~750m cores

The output of /stats/summary on a v1.26 node shows .node.cpu.usageNanoCores at  788,000,000 milli cores
 
