  I'm looking to figure out what changed

> an `UPDATE` doesn't work actually. the calling tree is:
> 
> * patchAllocatedValues
> * beginUpdate
> * store.BeginUpdate
> 
> it is triggered in the store definition and has no relation with how the request is hit on rest server.

that does not look right, the calling tree is no the important here, the important is the behavior implemented, and an UPDATE with the nodePort to 0 and the field AllocateLoadBalancerNodePorts to False IMHO should deallocate the NodePort, related discussion in  https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/91459, WDYT @thockin and @liggitt 

If that is correct, I think the bug is in the storage that does not consider the AllocateLoadBalancerNodePorts value, 

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/fa66a37fd9bdf4e56bc86695dbdf0c7484ba86eb/pkg/registry/core/service/storage/storage.go#L650-L655

If I patch that function to consider the spec field the Update deallocates the nodePort as expected

